, \"c\"};\n        List<String> view = Arrays.asList(arr);     // fixed-size view backed by arr\n        view.set(0, \"z\");\n        System.out.println(arr[0]);                  // the array changed too\n        try {\n            view.add(\"d\");\n        } catch (UnsupportedOperationException e) {\n            System.out.println(\"cannot add: \" + e.getClass().getSimpleName());\n        }\n\n        int[] prim = {1, 2, 3};\n        System.out.println(Arrays.asList(prim).size());   // List<int[]> with ONE element\n        List<String> copy = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(arr));   // real, growable list\n        copy.add(\"d\");\n        System.out.println(copy);\n    }\n}","filename":"Java"},"revision":1},{"id":"3fbc6032-d0f7-7628-b8c1-51cd63602c27","type":"code","position":"aF","content":{"language":"text","code":"z\ncannot add: UnsupportedOperationException\n1\n[z, b, c, d]","filename":"Output"},"revision":1},{"id":"f0e83abd-d24e-7ab1-b3d3-68c56e63a455","type":"heading","position":"aG","content":{"level":1,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrays are covariant (a design flaw)"}]},"revision":1},{"id":"944d047c-c396-7341-b3df-d9436cc1cd7a","type":"code","position":"aH","content":{"language":"java","code":"public class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Object[] objs = new String[2];      // compiles: String[] is an Object[]\n        objs[0] = \"fine\";\n        try {\n            objs[1] = 42;                   // runtime check fails\n        } catch (ArrayStoreException e) {\n            System.out.println(\"ArrayStoreException: \" + e.getMessage());\n        }\n    }\n}","filename":"Java"},"revision":1},{"id":"8f54893a-e0e7-7661-96ae-12be9a7d83c1","type":"code","position":"aI","content":{"language":"text","code":"ArrayStoreException: java.lang.Integer","filename":"Output"},"revision":1},{"id":"b58ad37b-1c73-7d2f-85cc-e55d3ad8c3c4","type":"question","position":"aJ","content":{"prompt":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","conten